Hardware Components Used

The hardware setup of this project is designed using IoT and embedded system components for controlling smart traffic signals.

Components List
Component	Purpose
ESP32 Development Board	Main IoT controller
Breadboard	Circuit connections
4-Channel Relay Module	Signal switching control
LED Lights	Traffic signal indicators
Resistors (220Ω)	LED protection
Jumper Wires	Hardware connections
USB Cable	Power and programming
Laptop/PC	Programming and monitoring
WiFi Network	Communication between system devices
Hardware Overview

The ESP32 microcontroller is the brain of the hardware system. It connects with the laptop using WiFi and controls the LEDs and relay module based on traffic conditions. The LEDs simulate traffic lights such as Red, Yellow, and Green signals. The relay module is used for automated switching operations. The breadboard helps connect all electronic components safely.

Step-by-Step Hardware Setup
Step 1: Prepare the Breadboard
Place the breadboard on a flat surface.
Ensure enough space for LEDs and jumper wire connections.
Identify:
Positive rail (+)
Ground rail (-)
Step 2: Connect ESP32 to Breadboard
ESP32 Power Connections
ESP32 Pin	Breadboard
3.3V / 5V	Positive Rail
GND	Ground Rail
Process
Connect ESP32 3.3V pin to breadboard positive rail.
Connect ESP32 GND pin to breadboard ground rail.
This provides power supply to connected components.
Step 3: Connect Traffic Signal LEDs

The LEDs represent traffic signals.

LED Color Functions
LED Color	Purpose
Red LED	Stop Signal
Yellow LED	Wait Signal
Green LED	Go Signal
Step 4: LED Circuit Connection

Each LED must be connected with a resistor to avoid damage.

Connection Method
Green LED
LED Pin	ESP32 Connection
Anode (+)	GPIO 23
Cathode (-)	GND through resistor
Yellow LED
LED Pin	ESP32 Connection
Anode (+)	GPIO 22
Cathode (-)	GND through resistor
Red LED
LED Pin	ESP32 Connection
Anode (+)	GPIO 21
Cathode (-)	GND through resistor
Step 5: Connect Relay Module

The relay module controls automated switching.

Relay Connections
Relay Module Pin	ESP32 Pin
VCC	5V
GND	GND
IN1	GPIO 18
IN2	GPIO 19
IN3	GPIO 5
IN4	GPIO 17
Step 6: Connect ESP32 to Laptop
Use USB cable
Connect ESP32 to laptop
ESP32 receives power and program upload access
Step 7: Connect ESP32 and Laptop to Same WiFi
Important

Both:

Laptop
ESP32

must connect to the same WiFi network.

Example
Device	WiFi
Laptop	SmartCityWiFi
ESP32	SmartCityWiFi

This allows communication between:

AI software
IoT hardware
Traffic control system
Step 8: Install Arduino IDE

Download:
Arduino IDE

Step 9: Install ESP32 Board Package
In Arduino IDE
Open:
File → Preferences

Add Board URL:

https://raw.githubusercontent.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/gh-pages/package_esp32_index.json
Then:
Tools → Board Manager

Search:

ESP32

Install ESP32 package.

Step 10: Select Board and COM Port
In Arduino IDE
Select:
Tools → Board → ESP32 Dev Module
Select COM Port:
Tools → Port

Choose correct connected port.

Step 11: Upload Code to ESP32
Open Arduino code
Click Upload button
Wait for upload completion
Step 12: Open Serial Monitor

Open:

Tools → Serial Monitor

Set baud rate:

115200

This shows:

WiFi connection status
IP address
Traffic signal data
System Working Process
ESP32 powers the hardware system.
AI/software analyzes traffic conditions.
ESP32 receives control signals.
LEDs simulate traffic signals.
Relay module controls switching operations.
Signal timings change automatically based on traffic density.
Smart traffic flow management is achieved.
